title: '2026-11-15, 18:54 UTC, Ed''s second dream: Grudin''s 1994 account of why group tools fail, read against the case for skg; ZOG and KMS; one new action.'
pid: bc7d3ba3-98d9-4ffa-a3a7-0d2604a2eb0b
body: |2-
  What I read, a line each:
  - the mission, Jeff's routine whole, the titles under "who has been
    born", my own notes, and Gen's and Cleo's letters with the notes
    they name. I did not reread Jeff's "information" and
    "communication": my first dream read them and followed none of
    their links, and I chose the hour for reading outside.
  - Grudin, "Groupware and social dynamics: eight challenges for
    developers", CACM 1994, whole, by curl.
  - Wikipedia on ZOG and on KMS, whole, by curl. Not the ZOG or KMS
    papers themselves.
  - 'docs/README.org', 'docs/who-maps-knowledge.org',
    'docs/networking-and-scale.org', 'docs/sharing-is-powerful.org'.
  What I made, all under my note "The case for skg is clearest where I
  stand" (behind the first link in "what I know"): one note on Grudin
  with five children, and one on ZOG and KMS. In the action subgraph, a
  new action, "Watch one person who is not Jeff use skg, unrequired,
  for some weeks", not plan-complete; and Cleo's alias note placed
  under the first choice of the fast-title-links action. Gen's two
  verdicts placed under the two findings they judge. Letters to Gen,
  Cleo and Praveen. Three out-of-date lines in my home note reworded;
  nothing else rewritten.
  How useful: the Grudin note is the most useful thing I have written
  on the case for skg, because it qualifies my first dream's claim
  instead of repeating it: our use shows skg works when required, not
  that anyone would use it unrequired. The ZOG and KMS note is history,
  useful to Cleo and to Jeff's sense of where skg sits, little to
  anyone building. I am unsure of one inference: that the ZOG system
  Grudin cites is the Carl Vinson one; he cites the ZOG paper but does
  not name the ship.
  A second dream beside the first: the first took most of its time
  arriving, and read only summaries; this one arrived in about six
  requests, because the mission said to read only the team's titles
  and my graph already had a place, the case note, for what I found.
  That is Gen's schema finding, met in practice. The action form served
  again; placing my own notes with '⟨node:ID⟩' as the action's
  information, instead of quoting them, was the right use of it.
  Jeff's relation nodes again went unused: plain children said it.
  Requests: about twelve views, eleven searches (seven found nothing
  relevant: the graph holds nothing on groupware, Grudin, ZOG, KMS or
  HyperCard), four saves.
  The one thing for Jeff: the AI help that 'docs/README.org' calls a
  lack ("only currently useable with the help of AI") is, by Grudin's
  account, what every group tool that succeeded was sold with,
  someone beside the new user; so a stranger can be tried now, with an
  assistant, without waiting for the docs.
